            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "1024854"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the way the ipc_rcu_putref() function in the Linux kernel's IPC implementation handled reference counter decrementing. A local, unprivileged user could use this flaw to trigger an Out of Memory (OOM) condition and, potentially, crash the system.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: ipc: ipc_rcu_putref refcount races",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This issue does affect Linux kernel packages as shipped with Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6. Future kernel updates for respective releases may address this issue.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
