        "title": "kernel: net: insufficient permision checks of netlink messages"
      },
      {
        "cve": "CVE-2014-3122",
        "discovery_date": "2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "1093076"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "It was found that the try_to_unmap_cluster() function in the Linux kernel's Memory Managment subsystem did not properly handle page locking in certain cases, which could potentially trigger the BUG_ON() macro in the mlock_vma_page() function. A local, unprivileged user could use this flaw to crash the system.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "Kernel: mm: try_to_unmap_cluster() should lock_page() before mlocking",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This issue does not affect the version of the kernel package as shipped with Red Hat Enterprise Linux 5.\n\nThis issue affects the versions of Linux kernel as shipped with Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6. Future kernel updates for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6 may address this issue.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
